The '''SCX 30''' is the benchmark {{w|stock market index}} of the [[Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor]], comprising the 30 largest companies by {{w|market capitalization}} listed on the exchange. The index is owned and operated by [[BdSC Corporació]], the parent company of the Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor, and is calculated using a {{w|Capitalization-weighted index|market-cap-weighted}} methodology. It is the most widely cited measure of Balboan {{w|equity market}} performance.

The SCX 30 was introduced on 2 January 1992 with a base value of 1,000 points, replacing the earlier Bolsa Composite Index as the exchange's primary benchmark. The index was created in response to the growing institutionalisation of the Balboan equity market in the 1990s and the need for a transparent, rules-based benchmark comparable to international indices.

