Energy is the largest GICS sector by market cap, dominated by [[CIEA]], one of the world's largest supermajor oil corporations, which alone accounts for approximately 30 per cent of the index's total {{w|market capitalization}}. The energy sector is complemented by [[Grup Tècnic Petrolí]] (GTP), the largest oilfield services company in Abyala, and [[Energia d'Abyala]] (EAB), the largest dedicated energy commodity trader in Abyala. Financials is the second-largest sector, anchored by [[Corporació Bancària del Nou Món]] (CBNM), the largest multinational bank in southern Abyala at approximately 17 per cent of the index, [[Banc Balboa]], [[Bitllet per a Abyala]] (BPA), the largest homegrown investment bank in Balboa, which has pioneered Abyala-focused growth ETFs and Global Depositary Receipts connecting Abyalan capital markets with [[Sanrobonia]], and [[Assegurances Heping]], the largest Balboan insurer. Materials is the third-largest sector and the largest by constituent count, led by [[Polímers de Balboa]] (PDB), one of the world's largest plastics manufacturers, [[Nutrició del Món]] (NDM), one of the world's largest nitrogen fertilizer producers, [[Companyia Química Occidental]] (CQO), a major supplier of polysilicon and semiconductor materials to Okaiken and Balisca, [[Grup Rojo]] (GRO), a producer of oxo alcohols, plasticizers, and polyethylene that competes with PDB in the domestic polyethylene market, [[Corporació de Plàstics Jala]] (CPJ), a producer of high-performance engineering plastics spun off from Grup Rojo, and [[Acereries de l'Istme]] (ACI), the largest steel producer in Balboa and the index's sole steel representative. The third-largest individual constituent is [[Coccola dels distribuïdors Abyala]] (CDDA), at approximately 5 per cent, followed by [[Abyala Telecom]] (AT) at approximately 4 per cent.

== Eligibility and methodology ==

The SCX 30 is a {{w|Capitalization-weighted index|market-cap-weighted}} index. Eligibility for inclusion requires that a company be listed on the Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor, meet minimum {{w|free float}} requirements, and rank among the 30 largest companies by {{w|market capitalization}}. The index is reviewed quarterly, with constituent changes implemented after the review.

The index is calculated in real time during trading hours and is published at the close of each trading day. The base value of the index was set at 1,000 points on 2 January 1992.

